---
import Icon from "../Icon.astro";
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import Rays from "./Rays.astro";
import "./nachtgestirn.css";

/** The air's shimmer: the Moon's lower limb through the air, and the air the light crosses, from the side. */
interface Props {
    id?: string;
}
const { id = "shimmer" } = Astro.props;
// Fried's parameter through one zenith column, in centimeters: a poor night, a fair one, a good one.
const R0S = ["5", "10", "20"];
---

<figure class="tiles-figure wide" id={id} data-shimmer>
    <div class="shimmer-row">
        <div class="tiles-panel as-seen">
            <canvas aria-label="The Moon's lower limb through the air, shimmering, rendered with WebGPU"></canvas>
            <span class="tiles-start">
                <span class="view-buttons">
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-part="motion" aria-pressed="true" title="The larger cells of the turbulence, which move patches of the image about as a whole">motion</button>
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-part="boiling" aria-pressed="true" title="The smaller cells, which make the image boil within those patches">boiling</button>
                    <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-part="colors" aria-pressed="true" title="The air's dispersion: it bends blue more than red, so the blue image stands higher, more the lower the Moon">colors</button>
                </span>
                <span class="view-buttons">
                    {R0S.map((r0) => (
                        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-r0={r0} aria-pressed={String(r0 === "10")} title={`Fried's parameter of ${r0} cm through one zenith column of air from sea level: the larger, the steadier the air`}>r₀ {r0} cm</button>
                    ))}
                </span>
            </span>
            <span class="view-buttons tiles-end">
                <Rays />
                <button type="button" class="view-icon" data-field="play" aria-pressed="true" title="Let the air drift on, or hold it" aria-label="Pause"><Icon name="play" /></button>
            </span>
        </div>
        <div class="shimmer-cut">
            <svg data-field="cut" role="img" aria-label="The air between the observer and the Moon from the side: the path the light takes through it, and how much of it" title="Drag the Moon to set how high it stands; double click for where it stands at the chosen moment"></svg>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="view-status" data-field="note"></p>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The air's shimmer on the Moon's lower limb, and the air its light crosses, from the side. The air between
        the Moon and the observer is a column of so many zenith columns from sea level, taken from the optical depth
        towards the Moon, so the observer's height and the air model count; the drawing beside it is not to scale, its
        bands holding equal shares of the air. How steady the air is, Fried's parameter r₀ through one column, sets how far the image of a 10 cm lens
        moves, as a differential image motion monitor measures the <Term of="Seeing">seeing</Term>: with the square
        root of the air crossed; the turbulence's cells, the lens' width over the distance to the turbulence, shrink
        with it; and the air's dispersion lifts the blue image over the red by a hundredth of the
        refraction. The larger cells move patches of the limb about, the smaller make it boil within them, and the
        colors fringe the limb, blue on top, red below. Drag the Moon in the drawing to set its height; a double click
        puts it back where it stands at the chosen moment.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import { shimmerFigure } from "./shimmer";

    for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("figure[data-shimmer]")) shimmerFigure(root);
</script>
